Optimal Solution - DP with hash maps to count the number of ways to assign + and - signs to reach a target sum.
                   Each number doubles the choices (+ or −), and DP maps help aggregate how many ways each sum can be formed efficiently.

class Solution {
    public int findTargetSumWays(int[] nums, int target) {
        // dp map: key = achievable sum, value = number of ways to reach that sum
        Map<Integer, Integer> dp = new HashMap<>();
        // Base case: one way to reach sum 0 (choose nothing)
        dp.put(0, 1);
        // Process each number in the array
        for (int num : nums) {
            // Map to store results for the next iteration
            Map<Integer, Integer> nextDp = new HashMap<>();
            // Iterate over all previously achievable sums
            for (int sum : dp.keySet()) {
                int count = dp.get(sum);
                // Choose '+' sign for current number
                nextDp.put(
                        sum + num,
                        nextDp.getOrDefault(sum + num, 0) + count
                );
                // Choose '-' sign for current number
                nextDp.put(
                        sum - num,
                        nextDp.getOrDefault(sum - num, 0) + count
                );
            }
            // Move to the next state
            dp = nextDp;
        }
        // Return number of ways to reach the target sum
        return dp.getOrDefault(target, 0);
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n * s). s is totalsum;
Space Complexity :- O(s).
